== THE CAST
------------------------------------------------------------

--- NPC: THE GARDEN GNOME ---
Wants: unknowable. Possibly nothing.
Secret: it is the most powerful thing in this chapter and does not appear to know it.
Voice / mannerism: does not speak, ever. Its painted face is either :) or :( and it
  changes between the two with a small ceramic CLICK. That is its entire vocabulary.
Opening line: (none - it clicks to :) and a bell rings somewhere for no reason)

  It is eleven inches of painted ceramic. Red hat, blue coat, gold buttons, one chipped
  boot. It does not walk; it is simply somewhere else when you look back.
  {THE GNOME IS YOUR PRESSURE VALVE AND YOUR PUNCHLINE. Once per scene, and any time
  the table's energy sags, roll on the Gnome table in the Appendix. Roll it openly.
  Let them watch you roll. The Gnome is a boolean oracle: point at a thing, ask a
  yes/no question, and it clicks to :) or :( - and it is ALWAYS truthful, but only
  about the literal question asked. This is a puzzle tool. The players will work that
  out in Act 2 and it will feel like their idea.}
  {It never helps in combat on purpose. Every Gnome effect in a fight is rolled
  randomly and may hit anyone at all. Except once. See Act 7. Do not foreshadow that.}

--- NPC: TWISTED ALICE ---
Wants: for it to keep being interesting. Nothing else. There is nothing else.
Secret: she is not a demon, a god, or a curse. She is a little girl who fell down a
  hole with an imagination and was never once told to stop.
Voice / mannerism: bright, polite, slightly bored. Says "oh, LOVELY" at horrors.
  Never raises her voice. Physically she is a nine-year-old in a stained blue dress.
Opening line: "You're new. Say something new."

--- NPC: THE CHESHIRE ---
Wants: to be alive again, and then to be owed a favour.
Secret: it was losing to her long before she killed it.
Voice / mannerism: arrives as a grin, then a face, then never quite the rest of it.
  Speaks in helpful sentences that turn out, later, to have been warnings.
Opening line: "Oh, don't stop on my account. You were doing so beautifully."

--- NPC: THE QUEEN OF HEARTS (the Heartless Queen) ---
Wants: her heart back. Failing that, a fair game, which she has not had in years.
Secret: without the heart she cannot feel anger, which was the only thing that ever
  made her decisive. She is now merely procedural, and procedure is a door.
Voice / mannerism: a cavity in her chest the exact shape and size of a fist. She
  keeps a folded handkerchief tucked in it. She speaks in rules and clauses.
Opening line: "Names. Papers. Or wait outside with the others and see what comes."

--- NPC: THE MAD HATTER (cursed) ---
Wants: nothing any more. He is a picture on a card that wants to be a person again.
Secret: he was the last one who tried to fight her and the closest one to winning.
Voice / mannerism: a laugh with no breath behind it. Talks in tea-party etiquette
  while doing violence. "Elbows off the table."
Opening line: "You're EARLY. Nobody's ever early. Sit DOWN."

--- NPC: THE CLOCKWORKER RABBIT ---
Wants: to be let go. Nobody has asked it what it wants in a very long time.
Secret: it is not Alice's servant. It is her second victim, and the clock is a wound.
Voice / mannerism: speaks only in time. "Late. Late. Nine seconds late. Twelve."
Opening line: "You're four minutes early and I hate you for it."

