=== SCENE: THE PARADOX CLOCKTOWER ===
Location: a tower that is taller inside than outside and shorter going up than down
Present: the party
Goal: two puzzles, then a boss. This is the longest act. Pace it.

[map:orins-tower-map|The Clocktower]

[READ ALOUD]
The tower is a clocktower the way a scream is a conversation.

It is perhaps sixty feet across at the base and it goes up until it goes out of
sight, and there are clock faces set into it at every height and every angle,
including several that face directly into the stone. None of them show the same time.
The hands on the nearest one are moving backwards, slowly, and confidently.

The door is at the bottom and it is standing open, and beyond it the stairs go UP.

You climb for what feels like ten minutes and arrive at a landing, and the landing
has a door in it, and through the door is the outside of the tower again, at ground
level, looking at the door you came in through, which is standing open, and you can
see yourselves about to walk through it.
[/READ ALOUD]

[DM NOTE]
THE LABYRINTH IS NOT MAPPED AND YOU DO NOT NEED TO MAP IT. Run it as a sequence of
four LANDINGS. The party experiences them in order. Between landings, describe one
paradox from the list. That is the whole structure - it feels enormous and it costs
you nothing.

PARADOXES between landings, pick freely:
  - They pass themselves on the stairs going the other way. Neither group is a copy.
    Both groups continue. Nobody feels good about it. If a player waves, they get a
    wave back, and it is not the one they gave.
  - A staircase that goes down to arrive above where it started.
  - A window looking out at the party, from outside, three minutes ago.
  - A room they have already been in, with their own footprints, and their own
    footprints leaving by a door they have not used yet.
  - A dropped coin that has not landed and will not land, hanging at knee height,
    slowly rotating. It can be picked up. It is very slightly warm. {It is a normal
    coin. It never lands again, for anyone, ever, including in their pocket.}

LANDING ONE: nothing. A chair, and a book on the chair. The book is the tower's
  logbook and every entry is in the same hand, and the last four hundred entries all
  read: "Still Tuesday."

LANDING TWO: THE ROPE ROOM - puzzle 1 below.
LANDING THREE: THE LANTERN BRIDGE - puzzle 2 below.
LANDING FOUR: THE RABBIT.
[/DM NOTE]

