=== SCENE: THE HOUSE ===
Location: Alice's layer
Present: her
Goal: establish the Notice track before anything else happens

[map:barrow-crypt-map|The Dollhouse]

[READ ALOUD]
You step out of a mirror into a nursery.

It is enormous - the ceiling is sixty feet up - and it is scaled for something the
size of a house. The rug is the size of a village green and the pattern in it is
rabbits. The wallpaper is yellow, with roses, and it is peeling in long curls high up
where nobody could ever have reached to start it.

There is a dollhouse against one wall. It is fourteen feet tall. Through its little
windows you can see rooms, and in the rooms there are figures, and they are people
you have seen: a woman with a slate; a man in a very tall hat; a queue of tiny
figures on a tiny road, holding tiny pieces of paper.

The far end of the nursery is a table. On the table is a shape under a white cloth,
long and low, and the cloth has been white for a long time except in one place.

And in the middle of the floor, sitting cross-legged with her back to you, there is a
little girl in a blue dress, and she is playing.

You can hear her doing all the voices.
[/READ ALOUD]

[DM NOTE]
SET UP THE NOTICE TRACK NOW, in the open, where the players can see it.
Put six tokens, six coins, or six tally marks on the table. Tell them exactly this:

  "This is how much of her attention you have. At six, she looks up. You do not want
   to know what happens at six. Yes, you can spend the whole scene watching it."

WHAT ADDS NOTICE (add 1 each, silently, and let them SEE the counter move):
  - Any loud noise: a dropped item, a fight of more than one round, a shout.
  - Any spell cast with a verbal component within 60 feet of her.
  - Waking a mimic without the Unmirror.
  - Being interesting: a magnificent joke, a beautiful lie, a piece of showing off.
    {Yes, really. Tell them this rule. It creates the most delicious tension of the
    night, because your players are exactly the sort of people who cannot resist
    being interesting, and now it is a resource they have to spend.}
  - Speaking her name aloud. Add 2 for this one.

WHAT REMOVES NOTICE (remove 1 each):
  - Complete stillness and silence by the whole party for one full minute.
  - Margaret's Thread, used on a character's own mouth {Appendix B}. Once per thread.
  - Doing something profoundly boring in her sight line. A player who has their
    character tidy up, count things, or sort objects by size removes 1 and deserves it.
  - The Gnome doing something so loud and stupid elsewhere in the house that it draws
    her ear. {You may offer this once. It costs the party their Gnome for a scene.}

AT SIX: she looks up. Go to THE LOOK, below. She will hit six eventually. That is the
design. The track is not about avoiding her - it is about controlling WHEN.
[/DM NOTE]

