=== SCENE: WHAT SHE IS PLAYING ===
Goal: the most upsetting thirty seconds of the session. Deliver it deadpan.

[READ ALOUD]
She has laid out a little scene on the rug.

There is a village made of blocks. There are perhaps forty figures standing in it,
each one about three inches high, each one beautifully made, each one with a tiny
black stitch across the face where the mouth should be.

She is moving them around. She is doing the voices - all of them, in a bright little
sing-song, one after another:

"Good MORNING. Good morning. Lovely day. Lovely day. Have you heard, have you heard.
No I haven't. No I haven't. Isn't it AWFUL. Isn't it awful."

She picks up one of the figures - a small one, a boy, with a hoop - and she looks at
it for a moment, and she says, in her own voice, quite thoughtfully:

"You're boring now."

And she puts him in her mouth, and there is a small sound, and she goes back to
playing with the others.

She has not turned around. She does not know you are here.

Yet.
[/READ ALOUD]

