=== SCENE: THE LOOK ===
Goal: terror. This is not a fight yet. Do not roll initiative.

[READ ALOUD]
She stops doing the voices.

The silence that arrives is enormous. The little figures on the rug stand exactly
where she left them, mid-conversation.

She turns her head. Just her head, first, over her shoulder, the way a bird does.

She is nine years old. She has a round face and a slightly upturned nose and a
smudge of something on her cheek. Her hair is fair and badly brushed and there is a
hairpin missing from it. Her dress was blue once. There are three buttons undone at
the collar and one of them is missing.

She looks at you with an expression of absolutely genuine, uncomplicated delight.

"Oh," she says. "Oh, you're NEW."

She stands up. The room does not get darker or colder or louder. Nothing dramatic
happens at all, and that is what is wrong with it.

"Say something new," she says. "Go on. Say something I haven't heard."

And behind her, every single piece of furniture in a sixty-foot room stands up.
[/READ ALOUD]

