=== SCENE: THE ENDING ===
Goal: the payoff for eight hours of a lawn ornament

[DM NOTE]
Do this properly. Stand up if you are the sort of DM who stands up.

Say, out loud: "Before anyone goes - the Gnome takes its turn."
Then pick up a die and roll it in the open, where they can all see, and it does not
matter what it says, and DO NOT LOOK AT IT. Then read this.
[/DM NOTE]

[READ ALOUD]
The garden gnome has been standing by the skirting board this entire time.

Nobody put it there. Nobody has been carrying it since the tower. It is eleven inches
of painted ceramic with a chipped boot, and it has been there for the whole fight,
and it has not done anything at all.

Its face clicks.

Not to a smile. Not to a frown. To something else - a third face, which none of you
have seen, which none of you knew it had, and which none of you will ever be able to
describe afterwards, and which every single one of you will try to.

Nine feet above Alice's head, the air stops being air.

There is no sound. That is the part that stays with you. There is a sphere of perfect
black about the size of a cartwheel, and it is not dark, it is EMPTY, it is a hole in
the fact of the room, and the light near it bends towards it and does not come back.

Alice looks up.

For the first time all night, her face does something other than delight. She has
just enough time for it - a quarter of a second of a nine-year-old girl looking up
and realising - and then her hair goes upward, and then she goes upward, and she is
drawn into it in absolute silence, all at once, without a scream, without a sound,
like water going down a plughole.

The wallpaper follows her. Then the dolls. Then the far wall.

The sphere hangs there, quietly eating the room.

And the gnome's face clicks back to a smile.
[/READ ALOUD]

